WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:08.113
[MUSIC]

00:00:08.113 --> 00:00:11.140
In this program of work,
we look at childhood obesity.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:15.420
And we look at this important
challenge for two major reasons.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.510
First, childhood obesity
is not just a problem for

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.840
developed countries like
we tend to believe.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.260
It is actually a great challenge for
developing countries as well.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:30.040
And this is because children in developing
countries tend to be both under nutrition

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.600
and over nutrition.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.290
What it means is that,
they don't have access to whole grain,

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:39.410
great proteins options,
vegetables and fresh fruits.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.680
But at the same time,
they have easy access to fast food and

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:47.590
sugary drink and those options tend
to be cheap and available everywhere.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:52.029
The second reason why we want to study
this is because childhood obesity actually

00:00:52.029 --> 00:00:54.193
has a long term negative consequence.

00:00:54.193 --> 00:00:56.417
For the children who are obese
when they are young,

00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:58.710
they tend to be obese as adults as well.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:02.840
This affects their long term health, but
also, their psychological health, their

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:07.680
performance at school, and potentially,
their social interactions with others.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.880
Obese children tend to
be bullied at school or

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.690
have a harder time making friends and
that could affect their well-being and

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.560
their relationship building.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.203
And because of all these reasons,

00:01:17.203 --> 00:01:19.703
we want to study childhood
obesity in this project.

00:01:19.703 --> 00:01:25.118
[MUSIC]

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:29.861
I work in advertising before and I'm now
a faculty specialized in marketing and

00:01:29.861 --> 00:01:33.470
I'm very aware that marketing
has been taken the bad name for

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.930
facilitating childhood obesity.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.990
So we see a lot of fast food or
sugary drinks,

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:43.590
all these famous brands using marketing to
influence adults and children's behavior.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:47.470
But what we are trying to do in this
project is to take a novel perspective and

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.790
to really think about what marketing is.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:53.840
Essentially, what market is trying to do
is to communicate certain messages and

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.790
to influence people's choice.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:59.320
So we could potentially use marketing for
the greater good of the society.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:05.841
[MUSIC]

00:02:05.841 --> 00:02:09.057
So we look at children in elementary
school from the first grade to

00:02:09.057 --> 00:02:10.050
the sixth grade.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.900
So usually that means they
are 6 to 12 years old.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:17.110
Why we chose the school is because
school is actually the environment for

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:20.570
these children for the very first
time to make their own choice.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:24.090
At home, they may not have a choice of
what they want to eat, their parents may

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:29.250
decide for them, but in school,
these children carry cash with them.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.010
They get to actually make a decision
of what kind of lunch they

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:35.030
want to eat today or what kind of
snack they want to purchase today,

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:39.140
without the immediate influence from
their teachers or their parents.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.090
So we believe that shaping
their behavior is important

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:45.830
because it is a very autonomous,
empowering decision for children

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:50.040
when they are choosing their own food or
drink for the first time at school.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:54.902
So this is a great place to educate
them what kind of choices they

00:02:54.902 --> 00:02:58.404
should be making that may be better for
them.

00:02:58.404 --> 00:03:01.568
[MUSIC]

00:03:01.568 --> 00:03:05.500
So in this research program,
what we did is we teamed up with UNICEF.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.030
So we work for several years together.

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:12.455
We launched a five different field
experiments in various schools in

00:03:12.455 --> 00:03:14.524
elementary schools in Panama.

00:03:14.524 --> 00:03:16.347
And that allow us to enter the school and

00:03:16.347 --> 00:03:19.230
try to communicate what is
healthy choice to children there.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.560
So what we did in one program is that we
basically used the print ad concept and

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:29.230
we used print ads to communicate
what is drinking clean water.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:32.900
So we educate and
promote clean water to children in Panama.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.280
What we found is that by telling it as is,

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.730
basically educating them that drinking
clean water is good for their health.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:43.249
Potentially, just having print ads in
school back grounds could be quite

00:03:43.249 --> 00:03:45.756
effective in increasing
their water consumption.

00:03:45.756 --> 00:03:50.442
And as a result, it could help to reduce
the consumption of sugary product.

00:03:50.442 --> 00:03:55.155
In another program, what we try to do is
to use a very typical marketing tool,

00:03:55.155 --> 00:03:58.930
price promotion,
to help promote healthy choices.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:01.860
And this is because we tend to
have a perception that all healthy

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.350
products are cheaper.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:07.474
So when we are trying to save money,
we may go with fast food or a cheap soda.

00:04:07.474 --> 00:04:10.820
And we tend to perceive
healthy products as pricier.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:14.080
Well, this might be true in some cases,
it is not always true.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:17.980
So we try to use price promotion as
a way to provide another incentive or

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.930
motivation for children to pick
healthier snacks at school.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:25.330
So we give them limited time price
promotion on healthy snacks, and

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:29.640
we track how much children actually redeem
those coupons to get healthy snacks and

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.510
as a result,
purchase fewer unhealthy snacks.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:36.010
And importantly, we found that price
promotions can even be effective for

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:39.350
very young children age of six to eight.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:40.030
Even for them,

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:44.470
they understand what it means to have
limited time to actually use a coupon.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.810
They understand the concept
of a good deal.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:48.180
And they may end up choosing or

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.360
purchasing a healthy snack at school
because this is on discount right now.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:56.556
And hopefully by trying the healthy
option, they gradually built the habit and

00:04:56.556 --> 00:04:59.066
preference for
healthier options in general.

00:04:59.066 --> 00:05:04.825
[MUSIC]

00:05:04.825 --> 00:05:09.779
This line of work can inspire and motivate
scientists from all disciplines to join

00:05:09.779 --> 00:05:14.443
us, because for me, I come from a
background of advertising marketing and so

00:05:14.443 --> 00:05:17.744
that is my tool for
trying to shape healthy behavior but

00:05:17.744 --> 00:05:21.660
we believe that long term change
requires more than marketing.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.725
We might be able to have price promotions
in a short run but eventually,

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:29.929
if we want to make sure healthy options
remain affordable and accessible,

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:34.539
we actually need more structural changes
on pricing the marketplace, tax, and

00:05:34.539 --> 00:05:36.530
government regulation.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:41.510
So we actually need scientist from all
different areas to help us accomplish this

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:44.210
and actually improve children's
health in the long run.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:48.706
So I hope that this serves an inspiration
to start a dialog on what we can do

00:05:48.706 --> 00:05:50.710
to help tackle this challenge.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:55.585
[MUSIC]

